<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat- Bids mostly higher.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat- Bids mostly higher.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring wheat cash bids were mostly higher on Tuesday in line with higher wheat futures.</p>
<p>December MGE spring wheat futures gained 3-1/4 cents to end at $4.34 a bushel.</p>
<p>&quot;It is still very quiet,&quot; a Montana dealer said. He noted the harvest of winter wheat and spring wheat is long over in Montana and that most producers were waiting for better prices. He said most farmers were eyeing $5.00 cash wheat.  </p>
